From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 07:44:39 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 274/297] Meridian: read Chrome's open tabs without the
 browser's session ids

Importing from Chrome (and Brave, Edge, Vivaldi, Opera) crashed with
"Check failed: HasCurrentDefault()" when Local State had no write
pending, e.g. after the person sat on the import step for ~10 s.
ChromeOpenTabs ran sessions::RestoreSessionFromCommands in the thread
pool; its SessionWindow/SessionTab take ids from SessionIdGenerator,
which writes Local State (UI-thread only) and starts its writer's timer
on a thread without a sequenced runner.

Replay just the commands open tabs need (tab window and order, closed
tabs/windows, navigations, prunes, window type) on plain structs, so
nothing touches the generator or prefs off the UI thread. A unit test
checks the result and that no session id is taken.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
